  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support life-saving WASH drought emergency interventions for vulnerable girls, boys, women and men targeting schools with linkages to communities and Health care facilities in Marsabit and Mandera Counties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of this project is to ensure schools have access to improved WASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene) services.  This FAO project provides access to sufficient and safe water supply for drinking, cooking, (through the school meals programme), personal hygiene, access basic hygiene services including WASH supplies/Hygiene kits, and adequate information to protect themselves from WASH-related diseases. In total, the project is targeting 15,000 children. 750 children with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
